# Scholea: optional account and sync backend (Supabase).
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored). Leave BOTH empty for the guest-only app:
# no account UI and no requests to any backend. CI builds exactly that way.
#
# These two values are public by design. They ship inside every web and desktop
# build. They are not credentials: by themselves they reach only the public
# sign-up, sign-in and emailed-code endpoints and the organisation's public
# settings. Everything else needs a signed-in account and goes through a
# database function, and each function checks its caller before it acts. No
# client can read or write a table.
#
# NEVER put a secret key (sb_secret_... or a service_role key) in any VITE_*
# variable: its text would be written into the built files. A build that is
# given one stops with an error.

# Project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# Local stack (`supabase start`): http://127.0.0.1:56321
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Publishable key (sb_publishable_...).
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
